Title: THE KOALA INCIDENT
Author: Anonymous Person
Contact:
    Sample script for Trelby.
    All rights reserved.
Agent:
    Nobody Nowhere
    Tel: 123 456 789

FADE IN:

At first, nothing. Then, a howling wind grows and grows in volume until it's painfully loud, while at the same time vague white movement can start to be seen, until it becomes clear that we're seeing:

EXT. STONEHENGE - NIGHT

SUPER: "STONEHENGE"

A blizzard rages. Snow is everywhere and visibility is almost zero. Only at brief moments do we catch sight of the stones forming the monument. No one in his right mind would be out in this kind of weather.

However, the rumble of engines appears, growing louder. A dozen huge trucks emerge from the storm and drive up to the stones. One of the trucks has a crane attached.

Men jump down from the trucks and start attaching heavy lifting cables to a stone, which is then lifted onto the flatbed of the truck beside it.

LATER

All of the trucks are full and not a single stone is left in the ground.

The men pile back into the trucks and start off into the storm. In a moment they are gone, and in place of the Stonehenge monument is just a few holes in the ground, rapidly filling with snow.

EXT. AIRPORT - NIGHT

A small local airport, with the storm still raging.

The trucks roll into view, smash through the gates and drive towards the runway, where a gigantic transport plane is waiting. As the trucks near it, it opens its rear cargo door and a ramp extends to the ground.

A truck reverses into the plane, where it has its pile of stones unloaded by the plane's internal crane, after which the truck drives out again.

LATER

All the trucks are empty and abandoned beside the runway. The plane's cargo door closes and the plane begins to take off. It is so heavily loaded that it just barely gets into the air before the runway ends.

INT. AIRPLANE CARGO BAY - NIGHT

Up until now everyone has been wearing heavy winter clothes and face masks, which they now take off. JASON, in his thirties, and obviously in command, climbs on top of the stone pile and addresses the crowd.

JASON
I want to congratulate you all on a job well done. It's now three in the morning, and the authorities won't notice anything's wrong for at least 3 hours. By that time we'll be in the middle of the Atlantic and they'll be helpless.

He looks at the crowd with a slight smile creeping into his face.

JASON
In anticipation of this moment, there's beer and other alcohol in storage locker twelve. I trust you know what to do with it.

The crowd cheers and surges toward the locker. Jason clambers down from the pile and heads toward the cockpit.

INT. AIRPLANE COCKPIT - NIGHT

KEVIN, in his forties, is flying the plane. Jason enters, followed by SARAH, in her twenties and stunningly beautiful. They lock the door behind them.

JASON
How long to the drop-off point?

KEVIN
About one hour, if the wind stays the same.

JASON
I'll go entertain the others so that they don't get suspicious.

INT. AIRPLANE CARGO BAY - NIGHT

SUPER: "ONE HOUR LATER"

The party is in full swing. People are drunk and getting more so. Jason is sitting with a group of people.

CREW MEMBER
What are we gonna do next, steal the Eiffel tower and sell it for scrap metal?

Laughter all around. Jason looks at his watch and gets up.

INT. AIRPLANE COCKPIT - NIGHT

Sarah and Kevin are in the pilots' seats, strapped in tightly. Jason sits on a foldout seat behind them and grabs hold of whatever he can.

KEVIN
Here goes nothing...

Kevin presses a button on the console.

EXT. OUTSIDE THE AIRPLANE - NIGHT

The rear cargo door starts to open.

INT. AIRPLANE CARGO BAY - NIGHT

A whistling sound grows into a roar as the cargo door keeps opening. Items tumble toward it, and people start to panic. Two people by the door are swept out into the air, their screams cut off as they disappear.

CREW MEMBER
Those fuckers are trying to dump us! Cut the control cables!

Gunfire erupts as people start randomly firing at the walls. Eventually someone hits something, as there's a spark and the opening of the cargo door is halted.

CREW MEMBER
Kill them!

The crowd starts running toward the cockpit, waving guns and yelling threats.

INT. AIRPLANE COCKPIT - NIGHT

They've been watching the events in the cargo bay on a monitor. They don't appear remotely worried at this turn of events.

KEVIN
Time for plan B.

Kevin pulls his stick back, sending the plane on a steep ascent.

INT. AIRPLANE CARGO BAY - NIGHT

Almost everyone falls down as the floor rises sharply. All kinds of items rain down on them from above.

A grinding noise is starting to be heard. Horrified, the people look up to see the huge mass of stones beginning to slide toward them. They try to escape to the sides of the cargo bay, but it's no use, the stones come down in a huge avalanche crushing everything in their way, including the cargo door which is ripped straight off.

EXT. OUTSIDE THE AIRPLANE - NIGHT

It's a stunning sight as the plane is climbing on a 45 degree angle, with a trail of stones tumbling out of its rear.

EXT. FISHING BOAT - NIGHT

SUPER: "THE MIDDLE OF THE ATLANTIC OCEAN - 04:00"

A calm night, with the ocean almost still. Two fishermen are smoking at the rear deck.

FISHERMAN #1
Aye, it's nights like this that make me remember why I love being a fisherman. Nothing but you, the boat, and the sea. Don't get any better than this.

FISHERMAN #2
I could use a bit more action, myself.

Suddenly, huge blocks of stone rain down on the boat, smashing it to pieces.

INT. AIRPLANE - NIGHT

Jason, Kevin and Sarah are standing in front of the emergency exit door, wearing parachutes, with a bright yellow package at their feet.

EXT. OUTSIDE THE AIRPLANE - NIGHT

The yellow package drops from the airplane with 3 people holding on to it. Within seconds of their exit the plane starts a steep dive.

The package and the people fall down. Just seconds before hitting the ocean they release their grip on the package and open their parachutes.

In the background, the plane crashes into the ocean.

EXT. OCEAN - NIGHT

The package hits the water and is submerged. A few seconds later, a rapidly inflating liferaft appears.

The people land into the water in their parachutes. They dispose of them and swim toward the liferaft.

INT. LIFERAFT - NIGHT

They're all aboard, taking off their clothes. When they're all naked, Sarah gathers the wet clothes, throws them out, and closes the entrance to the tent-like liferaft. The men openly admire Sarah's body, as she opens a storage locker and takes out dry clothes for everyone which they then put on.

KEVIN
I know a great way to warm up.

SARAH
Sorry, I got over the "older men" thing a while back.

KEVIN
Anytime you have a flashback, let me know.

EXT. OCEAN - NIGHT

The liferaft bobs in the waves, utterly alone in the world. Or maybe not so alone after all, for a small submarine surfaces just beside it.

INT. SUBMARINE - NIGHT

Jason, Kevin and Sarah descend into the submarine. The captain is waiting for them.

CAPTAIN
Welcome aboard. I trust everything went well?

JASON
Splendid. How many men do you have?

CAPTAIN
A skeleton crew of only five handpicked men who I'd trust with my life, just as you requested.

JASON
That's exactly what you're doing. If word of this ever leaks out, we both know I'm going to find you, no matter how long it takes. Understood?

CAPTAIN
Of course.

JASON
Ok. Now let's get going.

.MAP OF THE ATLANTIC OCEAN

A red line marks their progress southwest until it reaches Antigua.

EXT. SUBMARINE - NIGHT

Jason, Kevin and Sarah are ferried to a deserted beach by a silent rubber boat.

.MAP OF THE AMERICAN CONTINENTS

The red line snakes from Antigua to Dominican Republic, from there to Miami, and finally to Los Angeles.

EXT. JASON'S HOUSE - DAY

SUPER: "JASON'S HOUSE - LOS ANGELES"

A luxurious mansion with a swimming pool in the backyard.

INT. JASON'S LIVING ROOM - DAY

Jason, Kevin and Sarah are watching the TV which is showing a special report about the Stonehenge incident.

REPORTER
The British government is investigating several ransom demands about the stones, but so far they all appear to be fake.

The TV screen shows the monument site as it now is: A bunch of holes in the ground, surrounded by yellow tape and police keeping people out.

REPORTER
What possible motive could anyone have to destroy one of the oldest artifacts in the world? Police claim to have no idea.

Jason turns the TV off.

JASON
That'll confuse them for a while.

SARAH
So, what's next on the agenda?

JASON
We have a --

Jason is interrupted by loud cracks as three canisters shoot through the windows into the room. As soon as the canisters hit the floor, they start releasing some sort of gas.

Whoever is behind this knows what he's doing; the canisters were strategically placed at the exit points from the room. Jason, Kevin and Sarah have nowhere to go. They desperately try to get out, but each one passes out as soon as they come into contact with the gas.

> FADE OUT

INT. JASON'S LIVING ROOM - NIGHT

Jason and Kevin are lying on the floor, unconscious. Sarah is nowhere to be seen.

Jason seems to be slowly waking up. His eyelids tremble and eventually open. With a great effort he raises himself and prods Kevin until he too is awake.

JASON
Maybe they left Sarah in one of the other rooms. You check the upstairs, I'll check the downstairs.

2 MINUTES LATER

They're back in the living room, the search unsuccessful. Now they conduct a more thorough investigation of the living room, looking for any clues.

Jason notices the DVD player's tray is open and that there's a disc in it, with "WATCH THIS" written on it.

JASON
Looks like they left us a message.

He turns on the TV and closes the tray on the DVD player. A blank brick wall appears on the TV and a voice begins to speak.

KIDNAPPER
Hello. This is your new worst enemy speaking.

KEVIN
I hate him already.

KIDNAPPER
You are probably wondering who I am and what I want. The former is irrelevant, and the latter is simple: I have a job for you. Now, why did I not simply hire you? Because I knew you would not accept. Why did I not hire somebody else with lower standards? Because nobody but you can do the job. Faced with this seemingly impossible equation, I solved it by making it impossible for you to refuse. Impossible, that is, if you want to see Sarah returned to you alive.

JASON
I'm going to kill him if it's the last thing I do.

KIDNAPPER
What I need you to do for me is this.

The TV changes from the blank wall to a map of the world that zooms in on eastern Russia.

KIDNAPPER
There is a top-secret Russian research laboratory near Jelizovo on the Kamchatka peninsula. I want you to penetrate the facility, steal all of the koalas they have in captivity there, and bring them back here.

The TV shows a cute koala clinging to an eucalyptus tree.

KEVIN
Koalas? Is he fucking crazy?

KIDNAPPER
This DVD contains all of the details you need to know, accessible from the main menu. You have two weeks to accomplish the mission; after that, it's bye-bye Sarah.

KEVIN
Are we going to do this?

JASON
I don't see that we have much of a choice. It's the only way to have any chance of getting Sarah back.

EXT. FOREST - DAY

SUPER: "KAMCHATKA"

Jason and Kevin are lying on the ground at the edge of a thick fir forest, both wearing green army fatigues. Far away in the distance is an unremarkable looking gray building. Jason is watching it through binoculars.

JASON
He wasn't lying when he said the security at this place was almost non-existent. I see only two guards at the front entrance.

KEVIN
I guess the Russians don't have the money to spend that they used to.

JASON
It's also a way to avoid drawing unwanted attention to this place.

Jason resumes his watching.

JASON
We'll wait until the workers have left for the day. The place should be almost deserted at night.

EXT. RESEARCH LABORATORY - NIGHT

The two guards are standing in front of the building. Both have AK-74 assault rifles hanging from their shoulders.

GUARD #1
(in Russian)
Gimme a light.

The second guard lights the cigarette the first guard is holding out to him. Once it's lighted, he puts it to his mouth. As he's drawing the first hit of nicotine to his addicted braincells, those same braincells are splattered to the ground behind him as his skull explodes from a bullet's impact.

Before his body has managed to collapse to the ground, the second guard is shot in the chest in a similar fashion.

A few moments pass, then Jason appears in a crouched run. He checks that the guards are dead and then pulls out a walkie-talkie from his pocket.

JASON
The eagle has landed, I repeat, the eagle has landed.

KEVIN (OS)
Comin' in.

Jason drags the guards to the bushes and throws their weapons away. Just as he's finishing, Kevin drives up in a small truck and dismounts.

JASON
Ready to rock'n'roll?

In response, Kevin jams a clip into his AK-74. They take positions on both sides of the door. Kevin does a three-finger countdown and on zero, Jason pivots, kicks in the door, and charges in. Kevin waits five seconds and follows him in.

INT. RESEARCH LABORATORY - NIGHT

Jason and Kevin duck in and out of the various rooms full of esoteric equipment searching for anyone still being there at this time of the night, and find nobody.

They meet up at the animal storage area, containing about ten cages filled with koalas.

JASON
Look like perfectly normal koalas to me, but I'm no marsupial biologist. Let's load them on the truck and get the hell out of here.

EXT. RESEARCH LABORATORY - NIGHT

Kevin ties down the last tarpaulin on the truck. Loading is complete. He's about to start for the cabin of the truck when he notices something in the bushes where the dead guards were dragged to.

KEVIN
(shouting to Jason in the cabin)
Aw man, you didn't finish them off properly and now I have to do your dirty work!

Kevin switches his rifle's safety off and saunters to the bushes.

As he enters the bushes, instead of the crawling, mortally wounded guard he's been expecting, he's face-to-face with an enormous bear that's eating the dead guards.

The bear notices him, lifts its blood-covered head and growls.

Kevin makes a passable attempt at a new world record as he runs to the truck, jumps in, and slams the door shut.

INT. TRUCK'S CABIN - NIGHT

KEVIN
DRIVE!!!

Jason knows better than to ask any questions, so he starts the truck and drives off, gravel from the tires pelting the bear who's come up to investigate this strange new thing.

KEVIN
That was a fuckin' bear!

JASON
Oh yeah, did I forget to mention that Kamchatka has the world's largest density of bears? And they're also bigger than normal due to all the fish available here.

Jason grins.

EXT. HARBOR - NIGHT

Jason and Kevin finish loading the koala cages to a Japanese fishing boat.

.MAP OF THE PACIFIC OCEAN

The red line snakes along the Kurile islands to Hokkaido, and from there it arcs to Los Angeles.

INT. JASON'S LIVING ROOM - DAY

Jason and Kevin are sitting around, watching the clock. At the exact same time that it changes to 12:00, the doorbell rings.

Kevin stands up and disappears through a doorway. There's a sound of a door opening closing, and then Kevin and an another man walk in.

JASON
Where's Sarah?

KIDNAPPER
First things first. Where are my koalas?

JASON
They're in the garage.

KIDNAPPER
I want to see them.

JASON
Fine.

INT. JASON'S GARAGE - DAY

The koala cages are stacked around the edges. The koalas are mostly sleeping.

KIDNAPPER
No joeys?

KEVIN
What?

KIDNAPPER
A "joey" is what a baby koala is called. I gather they only had adult koalas then? Unfortunate, but acceptable.

JASON
I don't give a rat's ass about your koalas. You have 10 seconds to tell me where Sarah is before I kill you.

KIDNAPPER
My my, such hostile feelings. Try to contain your impulses while I describe my plans for these wonderful animals.

The kidnapper examines one of the koalas intently.

KIDNAPPER
You see, normal koalas only eat eucalyptus leaves. During the cold war, Soviet scientists started experimenting with imported koalas, trying to get them to adapt to eating any kind of plant matter and radically speeding up their reproductive cycle. They were not successful, and everyone thought the program was dead when the Soviet Union collapsed. However, 6 months ago, I received information that the program had been restarted, this time using genetic engineering techniques to directly modify the koala's DNA. These animals here are the first batch of the modified koalas.

KEVIN
This is ludicrous. Even if I were to believe you, which I don't, what are you planning to do with them?

KIDNAPPER
I'm going to breed them until I have tens of thousands of them, and then I'm going to release them throughout Northern America, thereby destroying its ecosystem and resulting in total collapse of the government!

JASON
That's the stupidest thing I've ever heard, but whatever rocks your boat. Now, this is the third time I'm asking you where Sarah is, and it's also the last, if you get my drift.

KIDNAPPER
Very well. I always keep my word.

He takes out his cell phone and dials.

KIDNAPPER
Bring her in.

He pushes a button on the wall and the garage door opens. A black SUV is just turning in and drives in to the garage. The front doors open and two men exit. One of them opens the back door, reaches in, and out comes Sarah.

JASON
You okay?

SARAH
Yeah.

KIDNAPPER
Now, I'm sorry to say, I have to kill you. I lied when I said I always keep my word. Any last requests?

JASON
Can I close the garage door? I don't like to disturb my neighbors with the sound of gunfire this early in the morning.

KIDNAPPER
(laughing)
Sure, go ahead.

Jason walks over to the switch and pushes it. The door begins to close. Jason makes a point of catching Kevin's eye, and clearly some kind of communication just happened between them. What are they up to?

The exact moment the door finishes closing, Jason presses another button on the wall. The lights switch off and heavy-duty shutters fall to cover the windows. It is pitch black.

For 10 seconds we see nothing, but the sounds we hear are somehow heightened. A metallic clink. A fleshy thump followed by a groan. A sick snapping sound. Silence.

A click, and the lights are on again. The kidnapper and his two henchmen are on the floor, their necks obviously broken.

JASON
Remember when I said I'd kill you? I always keep my word too.

KEVIN
What do you wanna do with the koalas? Do you think he was serious about them being a threat to the ecosystem?

JASON
Nah, he was obviously crazy. Let's just dump the koalas at the nearest forest. Some good samaritan will find them and call animal control.

EXT. FOREST - NIGHT

Sarah is opening the last cage. The koala doesn't want to come out, but eventually it sees that all the other koalas are already climbing trees all around it and doesn't want to be left alone, so it scurries off and finds a tree of its own.

SARAH
Now don't go destroying any ecosystems, you hear!

She heads back to the truck, laughing.

SUPER: "5 YEARS LATER"

INT. OVAL OFFICE, WHITE HOUSE - DAY

The president is sitting behind his desk. There is a knock on the door and his aide enters.

AIDE
They're waiting for you in the situation room, Mister President.

PRESIDENT
Tell them I'll be right there.

AIDE
Very well, sir.

The aide leaves. The president continues staring at the wall, then sighs.

INT. SITUATION ROOM, WHITE HOUSE - DAY

The room is full of high-ranking people, with a lot of army personnel present. The president enters and sits down.

PRESIDENT
Tell me you've found another option.

SCIENTIST
Afraid not, Mister President. All the lesser options we've tried so far have not been able to stop the koalas from spreading, so this is the only option left. We've already lost the four western states. If we want to keep the rest of the states habitable, we need to do this, and do it now.

PRESIDENT
I still can't believe we're even discussing this.
(looks around the room)
One last time: does anyone of you have any alternative ideas?

Everyone suddenly finds the papers in front of them in need of attention to avoid having to look at the president.

PRESIDENT
Very well. I shall go down in history as the bloodiest murderer of all time, but if that's what's needed to save the lives of over 200 million Americans, I'm ready to accept that title. Bring me the suitcase.

A man in army uniform steps over to the president and opens a metallic suitcase that's handcuffed to his wrist. There are two keyholes inside the case; he inserts his key in one of them, and the president inserts his in the other. They turn the keys in unison.

There is a moment of shocked silence, then people start weeping incoherently.

EXT. PRAIRIE - DAY

A featureless prairie on a clear summer day. Featureless, that is, until a gap appears in the ground accompanied by a loud rumbling sound. The gap widens, until it is a huge black hole measuring 20 meters by 20 meters.

The rumbling stops, but is replaced by a loud whining sound that suddenly increases to a deafening roar.

A sleek ICBM erupts from the ground and shoots up into the sky. We follow its path, zooming out, until we get to:

.MAP OF THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA

The missile we've been following was launched from North Dakota. Its progress westward is tracked by a red line.

It is joined by dozens, then hundreds of similar lines, from all over the map, all heading towards the western states: Washington, Oregon, California, and Nevada. The lines terminate all over the four states, blanketing them in pulsing red circles, until the whole of western United States is a slowly fading red color.
